            judgeFraming: 'Judges reward a student who can connect their method to its intellectual lineage — it shows the project sits in a real scientific tradition, not a vacuum. Naming Marey’s marker suit as the ancestor of reflective-marker motion capture, or Braune–Fischer as the first 3-D reconstruction, demonstrates you understand WHERE your technique came from and therefore its assumptions and limits. Getting the names and contributions right (and not fabricating citations) is exactly the kind of factual accuracy a knowledgeable judge will spot-check.',
