                    b: "Correct — the shear (braking/propulsive) claim exceeds what a normal-pressure insole measures; that claim needs a force plate or instrumented treadmill.",
                    c: "Insoles do measure force (normal pressure) — the issue is the missing shear components, not a total inability to measure force.",
                    d: "Insoles work during dynamic gait — indeed capturing many walking/running steps is their main advantage.",
