                    b: 'Correct — the CoM rises and falls, swapping potential and kinetic energy, which Cavagna showed recovers a large fraction of mechanical energy at preferred speed.',
                    c: 'The foot does leave the ground (swing phase); the pendulum refers to the single-support vault, not continuous contact.',
                    d: 'Air resistance is negligible and does not power walking; gravity-driven energy exchange is the mechanism.',
