                    b: 'Correct — pre-selecting features narrows the hypothesis before looking and ignores the rest of the waveform, so a difference at an un-extracted portion of the cycle is missed entirely.',
                    c: 't-tests are perfectly usable on scalars; the issue is that reducing a curve to one scalar loses information, not that the test is invalid.',
                    d: 'The weakness is statistical/conceptual, unrelated to whether a force plate was used.',
