                      b: 'Correct — Lance (1980) defined spasticity as a velocity-dependent increase in the tonic stretch reflex, which is exactly why the Tardieu test compares slow vs. fast stretch.',
                      c: 'Weakness is under-activation; spasticity is over-activity, a different mechanism.',
