                      b: 'Correct — external moment ≈ GRF magnitude × its moment arm from the joint, so shifting the GRF line toward (or past) a joint shrinks or reverses the external moment, reducing the internal muscle force required.',
                      c: 'Contraction velocity is not what these postural tricks manipulate; they manipulate the GRF moment arm.',
