              judgeFraming: 'Judges probe Parkinsonian gait because its most important features are not in a single average curve but in VARIABILITY and EPISODIC events (festination, freezing) — so a student who reports only mean speed misses the point. Demonstrating that stride-to-stride variability is a fall-risk marker, that freezing is triggered by turns/doorways, and that external cueing transiently rescues stepping shows the sophisticated, dynamics-aware reading of gait that distinguishes a strong project.',
