                      b: 'Correct — an in-turned foot can come from twisted femurs, twisted tibiae, or spastic muscles, each needing a different operation; Gage argued 3D kinematics, kinetics, and EMG are needed to attribute the deviation to its true cause.',
                      c: 'Cerebral palsy is a non-progressive lesion of the developing brain; the lab addressed treatment planning, not disease-course claims.',
