                    explanation: 'Gage was the pediatric orthopedic surgeon who pushed gait analysis into surgical decision-making for CP; Newington Children\'s Hospital housed one of the first such clinical gait labs; Perry, both surgeon and physical therapist, authored the Rancho functional terminology and the field\'s standard textbook. Keeping their distinct contributions straight is exactly the history-of-the-field literacy judges probe.',
