                      b: 'Correct — a before/after change with no control cannot separate the effect of the gait analysis from the effect of the surgery, natural growth, or maturation; you need a comparison group planned without gait analysis.',
                      c: 'Uncontrolled pre/post studies sit LOW in the evidence hierarchy, below controlled and randomized designs.',
