                      b: 'Correct — cost rises with amputation level (transtibial < transfemoral < bilateral), and dysvascular etiology adds further cost versus traumatic at the same level.',
                      c: 'Amputation levels demonstrably cost MORE than able-bodied walking; that excess is the whole phenomenon.',
                      d: 'This reverses the true order; higher levels (transfemoral, bilateral) cost more, not less.',
