                    explanation: 'The transtibial tax comes from lost push-off; the larger transfemoral tax adds the loss of active knee control; and the dysvascular surcharge at a given level reflects poorer cardiovascular reserve and comorbidity rather than an additional mechanical deficit — the ladder\'s two axes (level and etiology).',
