                    explanation: 'Suction is a passive airtight seal with an expulsion valve; pin-lock uses a liner pin that mechanically latches; elevated vacuum adds an active pump that both holds the limb and stabilizes daily volume; osseointegration skips the socket entirely by anchoring to the skeleton through the skin.',
