                      b: 'Correct — moment = force × perpendicular distance, so shifting where the GRF passes relative to the knee changes the moment arm and thus the moment, amplifying a small geometric change.',
                      c: 'Alignment shifts geometry, not mass; the effect works through the moment arm.',
                      d: 'Moments are directly governed by the GRF\'s position relative to the joint, which alignment controls.',
