                      b: 'Correct — a compliant heel compresses at contact, lowering the forefoot gently and reducing the flexion moment thrown at the biological knee, at the cost of a possible "sinking" sensation.',
                      c: 'The biological knee still responds to how the prosthetic heel arrests the limb at contact, so heel durometer very much affects the knee moment.',
                      d: 'Push-off is a forefoot/keel third-rocker function; the heel durometer governs the first rocker, not push-off power.',
