                      b: 'Correct — stiffer heels/keels give stability and support but resist progression, while softer ones roll over easily and return energy sooner but sacrifice stability, so the two pull in opposite directions.',
                      c: 'Cost and warranty are commercial factors, not the biomechanical trade-off the stiffness profile creates.',
