                      b: 'Correct — symmetry is necessary but not sufficient: a user can become more symmetric by degrading the sound limb, so a symmetry gain must be read alongside speed and metabolic cost to know it reflects real restoration.',
                      c: 'Symmetry indices are standard, accepted outcome measures — there is nothing improper about using them.',
                      d: 'Symmetry and speed are distinct variables; the claim is not circular, though speed must be controlled when interpreting symmetry.',
