                      b: 'Correct — metabolic RATE is per minute, but the efficiency measure is cost of transport (per metre) = rate ÷ speed; a higher speed can lower per-metre cost even while raising per-minute rate.',
                      c: 'Per-minute oxygen use is real data; it is just the wrong normalization for judging efficiency across different speeds.',
                      d: 'Faster walking generally uses MORE oxygen per minute, not less — which is exactly why distance normalization is required.',
