                      b: 'Correct — VO2 rises toward a plateau over roughly 3 minutes (the oxygen-uptake kinetics), so you average over the steady window and discard the transient, or a short burst misreads the true cost.',
                      c: 'There is no legal warm-up rule; the reason is the physiological steady-state delay.',
