                      b: 'Correct — CAS found the IAAF had not met its burden of proving a net advantage (and cited due-process flaws), which is different from proving the blades are neutral.',
                      c: 'CAS did not affirm an advantage; it found the advantage unproven, which is why he was allowed to compete.',
                      d: 'The ruling made Pistorius ELIGIBLE (for Beijing); it did not bar prosthetic athletes.',
