                      b: 'Correct — impulse (∫F dt) equals the fixed Δmomentum, so lengthening contact time flattens the force-time curve, lowering both peak force and loading rate.',
                      c: 'The momentum change is NOT eliminated — the body still stops its downward motion; only the TIME over which it happens changes.',
                      d: 'Gravity is constant; midsoles do not alter it.',
