              judgeFraming: 'Judges specifically test whether a student has separated stack height from drop, because the two are constantly muddled and they steer different mechanics — stack governs cushioning depth and stability, drop governs the ankle/knee load split. A student who reports both numbers, predicts the ankle-versus-knee redistribution from drop, and can cite the 40 mm World Athletics stack limit is demonstrating command of the actual design levers rather than repeating a "more cushioning is better" slogan.',
