              judgeFraming: 'Judges hammer the acute-versus-chronic distinction because it is where enthusiastic students most often overclaim — measuring one session and concluding "minimalist shoes are better/safer." A student who states their result is an ACUTE effect, cites the transition-injury evidence (Ryan et al., 2014; the post-"Born to Run" injury wave) as the reason a chronic claim needs a long graded study, and who designed the protocol to keep subjects within tolerance is demonstrating both scientific humility and research ethics — exactly the maturity a judge rewards.',
