                      b: 'Correct — pressure sensors read only the normal (perpendicular) component; shear forces, which are strongly implicated in diabetic tissue breakdown, are invisible to them, so a "safe pressure" reading is an incomplete risk picture.',
                      c: 'Step count is a timing/counting quantity, unrelated to the normal-vs-shear limitation being tested.',
                      d: 'Temperature is a different modality; the mechanical blind spot of a pressure sensor is shear, not temperature.',
