                    explanations: {
                      a: 'Stress fractures are not single-event overloads; they build up over many cycles.',
                      b: 'Correct — it is a fatigue failure where microdamage accumulates faster than remodeling can repair it, analogous to a repeatedly bent paperclip.',
                      c: 'Mechanical load is central to bone stress injury, though individual factors modulate risk.',
                      d: 'A stress fracture is by definition a bone injury, not merely a soft-tissue bruise.',
                    },
