                      b: 'Correct — losing protective sensation means the patient does not feel the pain that would normally prompt them to shift load off a repetitively high-pressure region, so the tissue breaks down.',
                      c: 'Neuropathy is a nerve problem (lost sensation), not a direct softening of bone.',
