                      a: 'This condition REMOVES/corrupts two of the three streams rather than providing all three cleanly — that is exactly what makes it informative.',
                      b: 'Correct — closing the eyes removes reliable vision and the compliant foam corrupts ankle proprioception, so balance here depends heavily on the vestibular system, isolating the vestibular contribution (people with vestibular loss fail it selectively).',
                      c: 'It does not isolate vision; it removes vision. It isolates the VESTIBULAR contribution by stripping the other two.',
                      d: 'It is the HARDEST of the conditions, the opposite of the easiest (eyes open, firm floor), not equivalent to it.',
