                      b: 'The reverse is true — if the COP moved less than the COM it could never overshoot and reverse the COM\'s drift.',
                      c: 'Correct — Winter showed the COP must overshoot the COM on both sides so that the COP–COM difference produces the horizontal COM acceleration that decelerates and reverses each lean.',
