              judgeFraming: 'Judges probe the XCoM because it is the exact concept that separates a project which merely restates the static "COM in base" rule from one that genuinely models dynamic balance. A student who can write XCoM = x_COM + v/ω₀, state that ω₀ = √(g/ℓ), keep the units straight (velocity ÷ angular frequency = displacement), and attribute the idea correctly to Hof\'s 2005 work demonstrates command of the field\'s central tool. A judge will often press "why divide velocity by ω₀ and not just add the velocity?" — the answer, that you must convert a rate into an equivalent displacement to compare against a spatial boundary, is the tell for real understanding versus formula memorization.',
