              judgeFraming: 'Judges deliberately ask "which direction\'s margin of stability matters most for falls, and why?" because a student who answers "forward" has missed the field\'s central finding: forward walking is largely self-stabilizing, and it is the actively controlled MEDIOLATERAL margin — governed by step width — that carries the fall-risk signal. Naming the correct direction AND the reason (no passive sideways stabilizer, so it must be actively regulated) shows a student has internalized the mechanics rather than a generic "more margin = better." Judges also test whether a student treats MoS as a signed quantity: confusing the sign, or claiming a negative MoS is "very stable," instantly reveals they have not understood the definition.',
