              judgeFraming: 'Judges probe sensory integration because it is where a student can show that balance is a FUSION problem, not a single organ. The signals of understanding are: naming the three channels, describing sensory re-weighting (and how foam/dark strip channels away), and connecting a specific loss to a specific behavioral tell — diabetic neuropathy → far worse in the dark/on foam; multifocal glasses → increased falls on stairs (Lord). A student who can explain WHY eyes-closed-on-foam is the hardest condition has understood that fall risk climbs when the last reliable channel is removed.',
