                      b: 'Correct — stride count, embedding dimension/time-delay, normalization, and algorithm (e.g. Rosenstein vs. Wolf) all shift the result, so two labs can disagree from methodology alone.',
                      c: 'They are the opposite of always-reproducible; that non-reproducibility across pipelines is the critique.',
