                      b: 'Correct — a gyro measures rate of rotation, so obtaining orientation requires integrating over time, and any constant bias accumulates linearly (drift), destroying absolute heading within seconds to minutes.',
                      c: 'A gyro works while moving — indeed that is when it is most useful; the problem is drift from integration, not a stillness requirement.',
