              judgeFraming: 'Judges probe "why did you put the sensor THERE?" because the site silently decides which of a student\'s claimed metrics are even physically measurable. The tell of understanding is a student who names the target metric first and derives the site (foot for ZUPT stride length, sacrum for CoM stability, shank for tibial shock) — versus one who defaulted to a wrist watch "because it was easy" and then claims clean per-step timing the wrist cannot deliver. A judge who hears "I chose the sacrum because my metric is a whole-body symmetry measure near the center of mass" knows the student matched instrument to question.',
