                      b: 'Correct — a loose mount over soft tissue lets muscle and fat overshoot and oscillate separately from the skeleton at impact, adding impact-locked ringing to the true bony acceleration.',
                      c: 'Gyro bias is a slow, steady angular-velocity offset, not impact-triggered ringing in acceleration peaks.',
