                      b: 'The accelerometer keeps working when tilted; the problem is that gravity is mis-projected, not that the sensor fails.',
                      c: 'Position is NOT measured directly by an IMU — it is doubly integrated, which is exactly why a tilt-induced acceleration error compounds.',
                      d: 'Battery drain is irrelevant to the mathematical growth of integrated position error.',
