              judgeFraming: 'Judges care about walking speed because it is the one gait number with hard clinical validation (Studenski 2011 tied it to survival), so they will ask both "why does speed matter?" and "how accurate is YOUR speed, against what?" A student who explains speed = stride length / stride time, names their estimator family (foot-ZUPT vs. step-length model vs. learned regression), and gives a validated error against a stated reference and speed range shows they treat speed as a measurement with an uncertainty — not a number their gadget printed.',
